# Copy to .env and fill in, if needed at all. Self-hosted mode (spec.md
# §13 decision 11, the mini PC) needs nothing here — the frontend talks
# to the API same-origin (relative /api/* paths) and Socket.IO connects
# same-origin too (apps/web/src/lib/realtime.ts), with no separate host
# or key to configure.

# Explicit opt-out for realtime (e.g. a test harness that wants it off).
# Leave unset/false normally — the socket always attempts to connect,
# same-origin, no further config needed; the 60s poll fallback in
# UnitsPage keeps the grid current either way.
# VITE_REALTIME_DISABLED=false

# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Cloud mode (spec §3.1) — dormant, not deleted. These only matter if
# apps/api's REALTIME_ADAPTER is set to 'supabase' AND this frontend is
# built against the Supabase realtime path instead of Socket.IO — not
# the case for the self-hosted deployment above. From the Supabase
# project dashboard: Settings → API. This is the anon/public key, safe
# to ship in the browser bundle (unlike apps/api's
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, which must never reach the browser).
# ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-anon-public-key
